---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { standardGates, tiers, tierCountWord, coldWallets, spendingWallets, disqualifiedWallets, gateByKey, wallets, walletsVerified } from '../data/wallets.js';

const floorGates = standardGates.filter((g) => g.level === 'floor');
const savingsGates = standardGates.filter((g) => g.level === 'savings');
const caveated = coldWallets.filter((w) => w.barCaveat);
const cleanCold = coldWallets.filter((w) => !w.barCaveat);
const cleanColdNames = cleanCold.map((w) => w.name).join(', ').replace(/, ([^,]*)$/, cleanCold.length > 1 ? ' and $1' : '$1');
const countByTier = { cold: coldWallets.length, spending: spendingWallets.length, disqualified: disqualifiedWallets.length };
const tierClass = { cold: 't-cold', spending: 't-spend', disqualified: 't-dq' };
const tierWallets = { cold: coldWallets, spending: spendingWallets, disqualified: disqualifiedWallets };
import RuleRef from '../components/RuleRef.astro';
---
<Base
  title="How we rate hardware wallets — our selection standard · BitcoinKeys.guide"
  description="Our published, opinionated standard for Bitcoin hardware wallets. Two separate judgements: a hard security floor a device must clear at all, and savings-grade criteria that decide whether it's built for cold storage or just for spending. Three tiers — Built for cold storage, Built for spending, and Doesn't clear our bar — with the reasoning for every device, including why Bitkey and Ledger land in different places."
  verified={walletsVerified}
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Our selection standard</p>
    <h1>How we decide what’s <span class="accent">worth trusting</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">Most comparison sites pretend every device is fine and let affiliate links do the talking. We don’t. This is a Bitcoin-only guide with an opinion — but a careful one. We judge every device on <strong>two separate things</strong>, and keeping them separate is the whole point.</p>
    <div class="axes">
      <div class="axis floor">
        <p class="ax-h">A hard security floor</p>
        <p>Non-negotiables about whether the security <em>model</em> is sound. Miss one and the device is <strong>disqualified</strong> — not a matter of taste.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="axis savings">
        <p class="ax-h">Savings-grade criteria</p>
        <p>What we want on a device guarding a decade of cold savings. A secure device that misses one isn’t unsafe — it’s just <strong>built for spending</strong>, not for a vault.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>That gives {tierCountWord} tiers. Every device is covered in full no matter where it lands.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="tiers">
    {tiers.map((t) => (
      <article class:list={['tier', tierClass[t.key]]}>
        <header>
          <h2>{t.label}</h2>
          <span class="tcount">{countByTier[t.key]}</span>
        </header>
        <p class="tagline">{t.tagline}</p>
        <p class="blurb">{t.blurb}</p>
        <ul class="tdevices">
          {tierWallets[t.key].map((w) => <li>{w.name}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </article>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>How we judge</h2>
    <h3 class="gate-h floor-h">The security floor — miss one and it’s disqualified</h3>
  </section>
  <section>
    <ol class="gates floor-gates">
      {floorGates.map((g) => (
        <li class="gate">
          <span class="gicon" aria-hidden="true">⛔</span>
          <div class="gbody">
            <h4>{g.title}</h4>
            <p class="gshort">{g.short}</p>
            <p class="gwhy"><span class="wl">Why:</span> {g.why}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h3 class="gate-h savings-h">Savings-grade — miss one and it’s “built for spending,” not disqualified</h3>
  </section>
  <section>
    <ol class="gates savings-gates">
      {savingsGates.map((g) => (
        <li class="gate">
          <span class="gicon" aria-hidden="true">❄️</span>
          <div class="gbody">
            <h4>{g.title}</h4>
            <p class="gshort">{g.short}</p>
            <p class="gwhy"><span class="wl">Why:</span> {g.why}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="callout">
      <span class="label">Why “more” is a problem for savings</span>
      <p>It sounds backwards: how can a device that does <em>more</em> — more apps, a helpful phone app, a company that can help you recover — be a worse choice? Because long-term savings and daily spending want opposite things.</p>
      <p>Spending money should be <strong>easy</strong>: reachable, forgiving, quick to recover if you fumble. A little complexity buys real convenience. But savings you’re locking away for a decade should be <strong>boring</strong>: a dumb, offline, verifiable lump of metal with almost nothing that can go wrong and no lifeline you don’t control. Every extra feature is another line of code that can carry a bug; every radio is another way in; every dependence on a company is a bet that they’ll still be alive, online, and willing in ten years. None of that makes a device <em>insecure</em> today — it makes it the wrong tool for the one job where simplicity <em>is</em> the security. That’s <RuleRef key="simplest-setup" /> in practice: the simplest setup that covers you wins, and complexity you don’t fully control is itself a threat.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Tier detail, BEST FIRST ──────────────────────────────────────────────
      The three detail sections used to run disqualified → spending → cold, while
      the tier cards at the top of the page ran cold → spending → disqualified.
      One page, two orders — and the cold-tier caveats landed last, where "all N
      devices above" pointed at the disqualified and spending devices instead of
      the cold ones. Reordered 2026-07-30 to match the cards (and /wallets' table,
      which also groups best first). The positional reference is gone with it. */}

  {caveated.length > 0 && (
    <section class="prose">
      <h2 id="built-for-cold-storage">Built for cold storage — and the caveats worth knowing</h2>
      <p>All {coldWallets.length} devices in this tier clear the floor and every savings-grade criterion. {cleanCold.length > 0 && (<>The cleanest {cleanCold.length === 1 ? 'pick' : 'picks'} — <strong>{cleanColdNames}</strong> — {cleanCold.length === 1 ? 'clears' : 'clear'} the bar with no caveat at all. The other {caveated.length} earn their place too, but honesty cuts both ways: each makes a trade-off worth understanding before you buy.</>)}</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <ul class="caveats">
        {caveated.map((w) => (
          <li class="caveat">
            <span class="cvname">{w.name}</span>
            <span class="cvtext">{w.barCaveat}</span>
            {/* THE FLAG ON THE RUBRIC PAGE, and this is the one placement that
                had to be got right. /standard is the page whose whole authority
                rests on the rating being a standard applied rather than a
                preference — so the flag appears here NOT as a rating, but as the
                proof that we did not quietly move one. A reader who suspects the
                rubric bends to events should be able to come here and see the
                device still passing, with our disagreement stated beside it. */}
            {w.notRecommended && (
              <span class="cvnr">
                <strong>Rated here, and not recommended for purchase.</strong> This device passes every
                criterion above and we are still telling you not to buy one today. That is a judgement of
                ours about the maker, not a criterion of the standard — we did not add one to fit the
                event, because a standard that grows a clause after each incident stops being a standard.
                {' '}<a href={w.notRecommended.anchor}>Why, in full →</a>
              </span>
            )}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  )}

  {spendingWallets.length > 0 && (
    <section class="prose">
      <h2 id="built-for-spending">Built for spending — secure, but not a vault</h2>
      <p>These clear the floor: honest self-custody, where the maker can’t take your coins and no firmware feature can ship your keys off the device. They miss a savings-grade criterion, so we’d reach for the tier above for money you’re locking away — while happily using these for day-to-day or smaller balances.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <div class="dcards">
        {spendingWallets.map((w) => (
          <article class="dcard spend">
            <header class="dhead">
              <div class="dtitle"><h3>{w.name}</h3><span class="vendor mono">{w.vendor}</span></div>
              {w.image && <img class="dimg" src={w.image} alt={w.name} loading="lazy" />}
            </header>
            <p class="dfails-label spend">Misses (savings-grade):</p>
            <ul class="dfails spend">
              {w.tierNote.fails.map((k) => <li>{(gateByKey[k] && gateByKey[k].title) || k}</li>)}
            </ul>
            <p class="ddetail">{w.tierNote.detail}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {disqualifiedWallets.length > 0 && (
    <section class="prose">
      <h2 id="doesnt-clear-our-bar">Doesn’t clear our bar — and exactly why</h2>
      <p>Fails the hard floor above. Still covered everywhere else on the site, because pretending it doesn’t exist wouldn’t help you — but we wouldn’t put your keys on one.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <div class="dcards">
        {disqualifiedWallets.map((w) => (
          <article class="dcard dq">
            <header class="dhead">
              <div class="dtitle"><h3>{w.name}</h3><span class="vendor mono">{w.vendor}</span></div>
              {w.image && <img class="dimg" src={w.image} alt={w.name} loading="lazy" />}
            </header>
            <p class="dfails-label">Fails:</p>
            <ul class="dfails dq">
              {w.tierNote.fails.map((k) => <li>{(gateByKey[k] && gateByKey[k].title) || k}</li>)}
            </ul>
            <p class="ddetail">{w.tierNote.detail}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="callout safe">
      <span class="label">The one rule behind all of it</span>
      <p><strong>Verify, don’t trust.</strong> A device earns the top tier by being something you can actually check and actually hold — Bitcoin-only, unable to leak your seed, open to inspect, doing one job, with a backup no company controls. See how each device measures up in the <a href="/wallets">full comparison</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .axes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.8rem; margin: 1.3rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .axes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .axis { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1rem 1.15rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .axis.floor { border-left: 3px solid var(--danger); }
  .axis.savings { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); }
  .ax-h { margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); }
  .axis.floor .ax-h { color: var(--danger); }
  .axis.savings .ax-h { color: var(--accent); }
  .axis p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }

  .tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 0.9rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .tier { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-top: 4px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .tier.t-cold { border-top-color: var(--safe); }
  .tier.t-spend { border-top-color: var(--warn); }
  .tier.t-dq { border-top-color: var(--danger); }
  .tier header { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .tier h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .tcount { font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .t-cold .tcount { color: var(--safe); }
  .t-spend .tcount { color: var(--warn); }
  .t-dq .tcount { color: var(--danger); }
  .tagline { margin: 0.5rem 0 0.6rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .blurb { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .tdevices { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .tdevices li { font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text); background: var(--raise);
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 0.4rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem; }

  .gate-h { margin-top: 1.4rem; padding-bottom: 0.3rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line); }
  .floor-h { color: var(--danger); }
  .savings-h { color: var(--accent); }

  .gates { list-style: none; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.65rem; }
  .gate { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; gap: 0.9rem; align-items: start;
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.05rem 1.25rem; }
  .floor-gates .gate { border-left: 3px solid var(--danger); }
  .savings-gates .gate { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); }
  .gicon { font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  .gbody h4 { margin: 0.1rem 0 0.3rem; color: var(--text); font-size: 1rem; }
  .gshort { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; color: var(--text); font-weight: 550; font-size: 0.94rem; }
  .gwhy { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
  .gwhy .wl { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }

  .dcards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.1rem; }
  .dcard { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem; }
  .dcard.dq { border-color: var(--danger); background: var(--danger-dim); }
  .dcard.spend { border-color: var(--warn); background: var(--warn-dim); }
  .dhead { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
  .dtitle h3 { margin: 0 0 0.1rem; color: var(--text); }
  .dtitle .vendor { color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .dimg { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 60px; height: 60px; object-fit: contain; }
  .dfails-label { margin: 0.7rem 0 0.3rem; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--danger); }
  .dfails-label.spend { color: var(--warn); }
  .dfails { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 0.7rem; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .dfails li { font-size: 0.8rem; border-radius: 0.4rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem; }
  .dfails.dq li { color: var(--danger); border: 1px solid var(--danger); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 8%, transparent); }
  .dfails.spend li { color: var(--warn); border: 1px solid var(--warn); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warn) 8%, transparent); }
  .ddetail { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .caveats { list-style: none; margin: 1.1rem 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .caveat { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--warn); border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface); padding: 0.9rem 1.15rem; }
  .cvname { display: block; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
  .cvtext { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  /* Sits INSIDE the caveat card, below the caveat, so it reads as one more true
     thing about the device rather than as a verdict overriding the rating above
     it. `display:block` and the rule above it do the separating — a colour
     change alone read as a second caveat in the same voice. */
  .cvnr { display: block; margin-top: .7rem; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px dashed var(--warn);
          color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .cvnr strong { color: var(--warn); }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .dimg { width: 46px; height: 46px; }
  }
</style>
